{"title":"1985 AJHSME Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many whole numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e8924412a12becf7905729885a46e3e351ec5a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> contain the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/0/fb0849b771d2cad0780f87e9d2a222734f89f58d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 100 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 120 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 137 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 140 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 148$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"423\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> numbers from 200 to 299 that have the number 2. In addition, there are 20 numbers that have a units digit of 2 and 20 numbers that have a tens digit of 2. However, we overcounted three numbers, 122,222 and 322.\n</p><p>Our final count is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92521d4bbf61834d5c7c81a2ebbd64e30071165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 + 20 + 20 - 2 = \\boxed{\\text{(C)}\\ 138}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"233\" height=\"28\" /> numbers that contain the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Complementary_Counting.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Complementary_Counting)\">Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AJHSME_Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Complementary Counting)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e8924412a12becf7905729885a46e3e351ec5a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> does not contain the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so only the set of integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f39a3242724f70e81d9037b59cca455b4794683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$399$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> need to be considered.  \n</p><p>For an integer to be between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f39a3242724f70e81d9037b59cca455b4794683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$399$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, the hundreds digit must be in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/62511f4d99c1621775385afa593225a56e41f220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> while the tens and units digits may be any digit.  So there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2d88c43fc0b2a6bac2946f8ec893f8897b6e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot10\\cdot10 = 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"125\" height=\"14\" /> integers in this range, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d233398613ec0c3398af649d643714e4044e9af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot9\\cdot9=162$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" /> of these integers do not contain the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d016f55154230b8ba5777af616b5dbdbf2b78000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300 - 162 = \\boxed{\\text{(C)}\\ 138}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"172\" height=\"30\" /> numbers in this range that contain the digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017191417\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 79/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3444/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20585:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017191417 and revision id 277529. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}